<title>GERMANY: Daimler shares off highs after H1 report.</title>
<headline>Daimler shares off highs after H1 report.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German industrial conglomerate Daimler-Benz AG traded off their highs on Thursday after the group reported first-half operating profit of 827 million marks, on the top end of expectations.</p>
<p>Daimler stock was up 18 pfennigs at 81.50 marks at 1008 GMT, off its session high of 81.80 marks.</p>
<p>&quot;Buy the rumour, sell the fact,&quot; commented one Frankfurt trader, who said the Daimler results were generally good.</p>
<p>&quot;These are certainly at the top end of expectations. There is no logical reason for the shares to drop,&quot; said another dealer.</p>
<p>--Catherine O'Mahony, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
